hus the ratio has no real zero-denominator exception in this domain. The actual outer tangent intersections and the half-step phase alignment are retained.\n\nThe proof compares the two cyclic area sums on one compact torus, cancels double Laurent coefficients, and matches the remaining simple residues. N=3, N=4 and N=6 are explicitly treated rather than passed through a generic argument.\n\n## Source editions, correction and credit\n\nThe exact source is arXiv:2004.12497v11 Table9, printedp11, with definitions in Section3.9. The shorter published companion omits this row. The later self-intersected paper's k806 is a different expression.\n\nThe neighboring arXiv k806,b row prints value2 for the same displayed outer/original quotient. Exact four-orbit geometry gives **1/2**: at a=5,b=3,c=4, the original inverse area is2/15 and the outer inverse area is1/15. This corrects the reciprocal value in that neighboring row without changing k806,a's constancy claim.\n\nThe inherited inverse-edge calculations from reviewed PRs #207 and #211, Stachel's canonical parametrization, and classical Jacobi/meromorphic methods receive explicit credit. This companion consequence is recorded as **already_solved, 1/5**, with no new-discovery or historical-priority claim.\n\n## Independent validation\n\nAn uninvolved separate reviewer gives **PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_TARGET**, with no mandatory correction. The reviewer did not author the candidate or either inherited proof and audited both dependencies in full. All eleven author files and four source PDF hashes match; both author receipts replay byte-for-byte.\n\n- Author: 22,496 exact assertions and 11,629 separately labeled80-digit diagnostics\n- Independent: 13,272 exact assertions and 16,281 separately labeled85-digit diagnostics\n\nThe finite and numerical controls support the complete analytic proof and are not substitutes for it.\n\nBinding hashes:\n- PROOF.md: 1d6573fbcd03e3ecb24fc3675ac4902fa3b14ae0ccbd9058bbd9dd6dd8a87e3b\n- Author 